<p><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-1128785" src="https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224604/default-7.jpg" alt width="662" height="1000" srcset="https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224604/default-7.jpg 662w, https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224604/default-7-238x360.jpg 238w, https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224604/default-7-159x240.jpg 159w" sizes="(max-width: 662px) 100vw, 662px"></p>
<p>Over 100,000 people move to the San Francisco Bay Area each year. Their motivations for doing so no doubt vary, but these days, the ambition to make a fortune at the epicenter of the tech industry — especially amid the rapidly inflating AI bubble — is hardly unheard of. Unfortunately, that desire can be so all-consuming as to crowd out any interest in, or even curiosity about, the city itself, to say nothing of its wider region. Yet the San Francisco we know today is the result of a story at least 250 years long, very little of which has much to do with venture capital or GPUs. Now, anyone who does want to make a start on understanding it can do so at the new-and-improved platform <a href="https://digitalsf.org/">DigitalSF</a>, with its more than 80,000 historical items <a href="https://digitalsf.org/">available to view and download</a>.</p>
<p><img decoding="async" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-1128784" src="https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224603/default-6.jpg" alt width="1000" height="801" srcset="https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224603/default-6.jpg 1000w, https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224603/default-6-360x288.jpg 360w, https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224603/default-6-240x192.jpg 240w, https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224603/default-6-768x615.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px"></p>
<p>An operation of the San Francisco Public Library, <a href="https://digitalsf.org/">DigitalSF</a> offers simultaneous access to multiple online historical archives. Search for the <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Golden%20Gate%20Bridge&amp;f=&amp;c=Archives%20of%20the%20City%20and%20County%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Digitized%20Book%20Collection&amp;c=Hormel%20LGBTQIA%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20Historical%20Photograph%20Collection&amp;c=Shades%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Book%20Arts%20%26%20Special%20Collections%20Center&amp;c=Government%20Information%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=Branch%20Archives%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20History%20Center%20Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1">Golden Gate Bridge</a>, let’s say, and the results will include hundreds of postcard photographs and other images capturing that iconic piece of infrastructure from a variety of angles and in a variety of decades, as well as&nbsp;— since this is the always climatically surprising San Francisco we’re talking about — under a variety of weather conditions.</p>
<div class="oc-center-da">
<div data-fuse="22871471544"></div>
</div>

<p>The same exercise would prove equally illuminating for <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Chinatown&amp;f=&amp;c=Archives%20of%20the%20City%20and%20County%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Digitized%20Book%20Collection&amp;c=Hormel%20LGBTQIA%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20Historical%20Photograph%20Collection&amp;c=Shades%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Book%20Arts%20%26%20Special%20Collections%20Center&amp;c=Government%20Information%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=Branch%20Archives%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20History%20Center%20Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1">Chinatown</a>, <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=pier%2039&amp;f=&amp;c=Archives%20of%20the%20City%20and%20County%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Digitized%20Book%20Collection&amp;c=Hormel%20LGBTQIA%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20Historical%20Photograph%20Collection&amp;c=Shades%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Book%20Arts%20%26%20Special%20Collections%20Center&amp;c=Government%20Information%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=Branch%20Archives%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20History%20Center%20Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1">Pier 39</a>, the <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Sutro+Baths&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1">Sutro Baths</a> (which weren’t always ruins), and&nbsp;the <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Ferry+Building&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1">Ferry Building</a> (which wasn’t always a collection of pricey shops). Inevitably, this sort of virtual tourism becomes a form of time travel.</p>
<p><img decoding="async" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-1128783" src="https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224541/OC-San-Francisco-postcard.jpg" alt width="1000" height="641" srcset="https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224541/OC-San-Francisco-postcard.jpg 1000w, https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224541/OC-San-Francisco-postcard-360x231.jpg 360w, https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224541/OC-San-Francisco-postcard-240x154.jpg 240w, https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224541/OC-San-Francisco-postcard-768x492.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px"></p>
<p><a href="https://digitalsf.org/">DigitalSF</a> also offers countless glimpses of San Francisco’s important periods in twentieth-century American counterculture, when the city made everything seem possible: <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=beatniks&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1">beatnik poetry</a>, the <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Grateful+Dead&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1">Grateful Dead</a>, a particular flavor of <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=punk&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1">punk</a>, the ascent of <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Harvey%20Milk&amp;f=&amp;c=Archives%20of%20the%20City%20and%20County%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Digitized%20Book%20Collection&amp;c=Hormel%20LGBTQIA%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20Historical%20Photograph%20Collection&amp;c=Shades%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Book%20Arts%20%26%20Special%20Collections%20Center&amp;c=Government%20Information%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=Branch%20Archives%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20History%20Center%20Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1">Harvey Milk</a>. But even before then, San Francisco had already experienced a disproportionately intense amount of history during its relatively short existence: the earthquakes of <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=1868+earthquake&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1">1868</a> and <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=1906+earthquake&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1">1906</a>, for example,&nbsp;or the <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=%22gold+rush%22&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1">Gold Rush</a> of the late eighteen-forties from whose participants the <a href="https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=49ers&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1">local football team</a> took its name. Those “forty-niners” who flooded in from all over the rest of the United States, turning San Francisco from a small port town into a relatively major city practically overnight, probably had scant fascination with local history themselves. After all, they were too busy making it. Enter the <a href="https://digitalsf.org/">DigitalSF</a> <a href="https://digitalsf.org/">here</a>.</p>
